        "date": "2026-11-07T16:52:30Z"
      },
      "message": "fix(app): refuse a drill R plane below the unfaced stock top by name\n\nAn axial drill whose R plane (Top of Part Z) lay under the declared stock\ntop generated clean and posted silently (G81/G73 R20 under a Z25 stock top,\nand the expanded G00 Z+20 chain): drill_reach clipped the stock to R and\nverify's rapid law skips every vertical rapid, so the rapid down to R\nthrough uncut stock reached the post - a collision.\n\ndrill_reach now refuses, per cycle, any raw stock above the R plane over\nthe tool's body disk, by name, and the reach and holder laws read the\nstock unclipped. Faced stock still counts at its raw height until #89.\nFixtures whose own declared stock stood over their R plane (lathe axial\ndrill, the Z-only cross file test) now sit their stock or R honestly; the\nlathe golden is unchanged. The verify-side net is held as #96.\n\nFixes #91\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
