      },
      "message": "fix(app): drill R-plane review fixes - part as material, plane max over the disk\n\n- The R-plane law reads the part (its facets over the body disk and the\n  hole's entry surface) together with the stock: with no stock, or the\n  stock as the op's source, it no longer gets an empty slice - a\n  stockless R under the part top is refused, naming \"the part top\".\n- A facet counts at its plane's maximum over the disk (clipped to the\n  circumscribing octagon), not its highest vertex: a drafted stock top\n  no longer refuses an honest R or names the far vertex's height. The\n  reach and holder laws share the reader. The readers move to\n  operation/drill_top.rs (drill_reach under 400 lines).\n- Seeding unchanged (Top of Stock has no stockless fallback and the seed\n  has no world); the UX cost recorded in RECOMMENDED.md.\n- drill_rplane: the post-path refusal asserts its words; Spot/Tap/Bore,\n  a hole beside the stock footprint, R from Top of Stock, stockless and\n  drafted cases added. drilling_cross's Z-only fixture asserts Ok.\n  operations' staleness fixture moved the part up under its fixed R (a\n  real refusal now); it moves down instead.\n\nRefs #91\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
